## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] nums, int k) {
        // Initialise
        int longestOne = 0, left = 0, zeroCount = 0;

        //Sliding Window
        for( int right=0; right < nums.length; right++ ) { 
            if ( nums[right] == 0) {
                zeroCount ++;
            }
            while ( zeroCount > k ) {
                //Check the left position as 0
                // if 0, then move the window by one length 
                if( nums[left] == 0) {
                    zeroCount --;
                }
                left++;
            }

            //find the max between the pre existing and length of window
            longestOne = Math.max(longestOne, right-left+1);
        }
        return longestOne;
    }
}
```

